AMD FidelityFX SDK, vendored: FSR 3.1 upscaler + Vulkan backend
================================================================

SDK version : 1.1.4  (FSR 3 upscaler component 3.1.4, ffxFsr3UpscalerGetEffectVersion)
Source      : https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/FidelityFX-SDK
Tag         : v1.1.4, commit c6efa6bf7f2027b3ec94f28578bb5965eabb9e55 (shallow clone, depth 1)
Vendored on : 2026-10-19
License     : MIT, (C) 2024 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. (LICENSE.txt). Every vendored file keeps its AMD header.
Frozen copy : v1.1.4 is the last SDK release with a Vulkan backend (v2.x lists Vulkan as unsupported). We own any fix.

What is vendored
----------------
Only the upscaler. Frame interpolation, optical flow, the frame-interpolation swapchain, the DX12 backend, the other effects
(FSR1/FSR2 old component, CAS, SPD host side, ...), the FFX API DLL layer (ffx-api/), samples and the framework are NOT here.
Paths mirror sdk/ in the SDK repository. Files are byte-identical to the tag except ffx/src/backends/vk/ffx_vk.cpp and
ffx_fsr3upscaler_callbacks_glsl.h (see below).

Sizes in bytes. 55 files from AMD (1,207,710 bytes) plus tools/ffx_blobgen.cpp (ours).

